cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PHON in your research, please cite this repository."
title: "PHON: A Domain-Specific Language for Photonic Circuit Design and Optical Neural Network Inference"
abstract: >-
  PHON is an open-source DSL for photonic circuit design and optical neural network inference. A single source compiles to simulation, GDSII layout export, and (as of v0.10.0) neural network inference via layer/propagate primitives with numpy-backed matmul.
  v0.10.0 supports photonic (optical) media; phononic (acoustic) support is planned for Phase 5.5 via a unified `medium kind` attribute, which will dispatch physics constants (refractive index, sound velocity) without changing the computation.
  v0.10.0 simulates on CPU; physical deployment (photonic chips, SAW devices) is future work. A companion pipeline (PHON-LLM, separate repository) provides natural-language frontends: 135M LoRA-tuned code generation with constrained decoding (98% syntax validity) and hybrid parameter extraction (regex + Qwen-0.5B/Outlines CFG, 100% on curated and novel eval sets).
  Phase 5 (v0.10.0) achieves 97.78% MNIST test accuracy with 0 mismatches versus scikit-learn predictions on a 100-sample audit set.
